// The only reason this file exists: zenoh-bridge-ros2dds v1.9.0 has no CLI
// flag for connect-retry behaviour -- `-c <file>` is its only config override
// (there is no --cfg). Zenoh's client-mode defaults are connect.timeout_ms 0
// and exit_on_failure true, so the bridge gives up and exits about 10s after
// start if the router is unreachable -- which is the normal case whenever the
// robot boots before the server. Verified against the 1.9.0 image: without
// these two keys the process logs "Failed to start Zenoh runtime ... Exiting";
// with them it waits, and attaches as soon as the router appears.
//
// Everything else -- mode, endpoint, namespace -- stays on the command line in
// docker-compose.yml, because those are per-robot values that come from .env.
{
  connect: {
    timeout_ms: -1,
    exit_on_failure: false,
  },
}
